1.The HTML Document Object Model (DOM) is a tree structure, where each HTML tag becomes a node in the hierarchy.

2.At the top, the <html> tag is the root element, containing both <head> and<body> as child elements.

3.These in turn have their own children, such as <title>, <div>, and nested elements like <h1>, <p>,<ul>, and <li>.

4.Elements that contain other elements are labeled as container elements, while elements that do not are simply child elements.

5.This hierarchy allows developers to navigate and manipulate web page content using JavaScript by traversing from parent to child and vice versa.       


